  "pieces_note": "head = the bucket helm with its ring and visor slit (front only), rigid; torso with the hood-and-scarf cowl fused in (rigid; the cowl covers both shoulder joints, so no cowl pixel may belong to an arm); pelvis with the belt and buckle fused in; tabard = the oxblood panel with its tower emblem (front only) as a skinned cloth chain on pelvis (tabard_mid, tabard_tip; at most 3 px follow-through); coat_near and coat_far = the ragged gambeson tails as skinned cloth chains on pelvis (coat_near_mid, coat_near_tip, coat_far_mid, coat_far_tip; at most 4 px follow-through, settled by clip end); per arm a skinned root limb over upper and fore (the leather bands ride the forearm) with the gloved fist as a rigid hand; chain = the chain and hook as one rigid held item in hand_far, pivot at the grip, hanging at rest; per leg a skinned root leg and a rigid boot. Hidden fills (spec §1, the rr-37 lesson): every area a moving arm, fist, chain or coat tail uncovers shows its covered piece's own painted continuation: the torso flank under each arm's full rest footprint, the near coat tail and trousers under the near fist and forearm, the cowl under the raised chain arm.",
